WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.070
Set a compass on the bench.

2
00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:06.080
Its north end points along the
magnetic field where it sits.

3
00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:09.700
Now hold a long straight
wire just above the needle,

4
00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:12.610
lined up with it, and switch on a current.

5
00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:15.840
Moving charges make a
magnetic field of their own.

6
00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:19.780
And a current is exactly
that: charge on the move.

7
00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:22.260
So does the needle move at all?

8
00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:25.930
If it does, which way
does it turn, and why?

9
00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:29.010
In this mission, you'll
learn to read field lines:

10
00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:32.030
their direction, and what crowding means.

11
00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:36.610
Then you'll use one rule for your right
hand to map the fields of a straight wire,

12
00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:39.240
a flat coil and a long coil.

13
00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:42.310
Your mission: predict
which way the needle turns,

14
00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:43.650
and explain why.
